{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And accepted by the majority of his brethren.</b> For it is impossible for a person to please everyone, on account of the jealousy of brethren." "<b>Seeking good for his people.</b> It suffices that he do good to whomever among his people seeks it of him. Yet he himself sought to do good. And his seed — they are his sons and his sons' sons — and sons always fear their father. And he was one who spoke peace at the outset, even to his sons who are like his servants, and all the more so to his people. And so Scripture mentions the greatness of his rank and his humility, just as Scripture mentions the like regarding Moses our master: 'Now the man Moses was very humble, more than any man'."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:29.755651034Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}